1
00:00:00,567 --> 00:00:01,267
<i> We are wasting time.</i>

2
00:00:01,400 --> 00:00:02,033
<i> Don't forget, Joey.</i>

3
00:00:02,300 --> 00:00:03,800
<i> Blood is thicker than water.</i>

4
00:00:03,933 --> 00:00:05,000
<i> What do you mean?</i>

5
00:00:05,133 --> 00:00:06,867
<i> Andrew is related to Berdugo?</i>

6
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:08,533
<i>I always stand on
the side of truth,</i>

7
00:00:08,667 --> 00:00:10,133
<i> even if my enemy is family.</i>

8
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:11,500
<i> This is what we need.</i>

9
00:00:11,633 --> 00:00:14,100
<i>Because Tomas Limjoco
is the real Berdugo.</i>

10
00:00:14,233 --> 00:00:16,700
<i>We're going to the rest house
to visit mommy.</i>

11
00:00:16,833 --> 00:00:17,767
<i> I'll go with you guys.</i>

12
00:00:17,900 --> 00:00:19,167
<i> This isn't true, Andrew.</i>

13
00:00:19,300 --> 00:00:20,433
<i> This isn't true.</i>

14
00:00:20,567 --> 00:00:23,000
<i>I'm sorry, Yvette,
but we don't have time.</i>

15
00:00:23,133 --> 00:00:24,300
<i> We need to act now.</i>

16
00:00:24,433 --> 00:00:26,200
<i> Tomas went with them.</i>

17
00:00:26,333 --> 00:00:27,800
<i> Andrew, you go in first.</i>

18
00:00:27,933 --> 00:00:29,267
<i> Secure your family.</i>

19
00:00:29,400 --> 00:00:30,867
<i> Joey, you'll accompany them.</i>

20
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:32,633
<i> And you, Jin Ho, come with us.</i>

21
00:00:32,767 --> 00:00:35,367
<i>You'll identify
if Tomas is Berdugo.</i>

22
00:00:35,533 --> 00:00:36,800
<i> Where is Yvette? Where?</i>

23
00:00:36,933 --> 00:00:40,567
<i>They're inside,
but Sir Tomas has a gun!</i>

24
00:00:40,700 --> 00:00:43,433
<i> [GUNS FIRING]</i>

25
00:00:43,567 --> 00:00:45,033
<i> Dad...</i>

26
00:00:47,467 --> 00:00:49,733
<i> [OBB]</i>

27
00:01:03,533 --> 00:01:05,000
Dad...
[MULTIPLE GUNFIRE]

28
00:01:05,133 --> 00:01:06,267
Something might have happened
to dad.

29
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:08,433
I'll call you later, Peter!

30
00:01:08,600 --> 00:01:10,433
Joey, wait...
[PHONE BEEPING]

31
00:01:10,567 --> 00:01:12,500
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

32
00:01:12,633 --> 00:01:14,667
Major, are you okay?

33
00:01:14,800 --> 00:01:16,433
Thank you.

34
00:01:18,033 --> 00:01:21,033
[GUNS FIRING]

35
00:01:21,167 --> 00:01:22,467
My hunch was right.

36
00:01:22,600 --> 00:01:24,267
He figured out our plan, Major.

37
00:01:24,400 --> 00:01:26,800
All units, we need backup!

38
00:01:26,933 --> 00:01:29,700
I repeat, we need backup!

39
00:01:29,833 --> 00:01:33,867
[GUNS FIRING]

40
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:35,700
Tomas Limjoco!

41
00:01:36,233 --> 00:01:37,400
Surrender now!

42
00:01:37,533 --> 00:01:39,533
We know your true identity!

43
00:01:40,033 --> 00:01:41,467
Tomas!

44
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:44,000
We know you're Berdugo!

45
00:01:44,133 --> 00:01:45,500
Go ahead and try!

46
00:01:45,633 --> 00:01:48,067
We'll kill all
the hostages here!

47
00:01:49,833 --> 00:01:51,400
The rest of you, stay here.

48
00:01:51,533 --> 00:01:52,967
You two, follow me.

49
00:01:53,100 --> 00:01:54,733
Yes, Sir! Let's go!

50
00:01:54,867 --> 00:01:57,500
[GUNS FIRING]

51
00:01:57,633 --> 00:02:00,900
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

52
00:02:07,533 --> 00:02:11,800
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

53
00:02:16,733 --> 00:02:17,767
Hello, Dad?

54
00:02:17,900 --> 00:02:20,033
What's happening? Are you okay?

55
00:02:20,167 --> 00:02:22,633
<i> Joey, we've been discovered.</i>

56
00:02:22,767 --> 00:02:24,867
Don't leave that spot,
it's dangerous.

57
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:29,367
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

58
00:02:31,867 --> 00:02:35,900
[PEOPLE CRYING]

59
00:02:37,800 --> 00:02:39,500
Dad, why are you doing this
to us?

60
00:02:39,633 --> 00:02:42,000
Daddy!

61
00:02:42,133 --> 00:02:44,333
Take the children
to the other room.

62
00:02:44,467 --> 00:02:46,433
[KISSES BAWLING]
What are you doing!

63
00:02:46,567 --> 00:02:49,633
[CLAMORING]
Tomas! Don't!

64
00:02:50,433 --> 00:02:52,400
Don't! Tomas!

65
00:02:52,533 --> 00:02:54,567
No! No!

66
00:02:54,700 --> 00:02:55,800
Tomas, what are you doing?

67
00:02:55,933 --> 00:02:58,267
- Tomas!
- Tomas, stop!

68
00:02:58,400 --> 00:03:02,000
Don't drag your family
into your viciousness!

69
00:03:02,133 --> 00:03:03,767
What's wrong with you?

70
00:03:04,233 --> 00:03:05,300
[SLAPS]

71
00:03:05,433 --> 00:03:06,667
Tomas!

72
00:03:06,800 --> 00:03:09,567
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

73
00:03:09,700 --> 00:03:11,467
Tomas, don't!

74
00:03:11,600 --> 00:03:13,800
Tomas, please.

75
00:03:18,433 --> 00:03:21,433
How dare you betray me?

76
00:03:23,933 --> 00:03:26,167
You think I wouldn't sense it?

77
00:03:27,333 --> 00:03:29,900
<i> Hon, we're here.</i>

78
00:03:30,033 --> 00:03:31,633
<i> Who were you talking to?</i>

79
00:03:31,767 --> 00:03:32,800
<i> It's Andrew.</i>

80
00:03:32,933 --> 00:03:35,200
<i>I told him to come here
so we can be together.</i>

81
00:03:35,333 --> 00:03:37,233
<i>Go out to grandmother's garden,
okay?</i>

82
00:03:37,367 --> 00:03:39,333
<i>But didn't you say
we shouldn't go out, Mommy?</i>

83
00:03:39,467 --> 00:03:41,333
<i>You could, just for today.
It's okay.</i>

84
00:03:41,467 --> 00:03:42,300
<i> Isn't it hot outside?</i>

85
00:03:42,433 --> 00:03:44,200
<i> It's good for mommy too...</i>

86
00:03:44,333 --> 00:03:46,333
<i> so she can breathe fresh air.</i>

87
00:03:46,467 --> 00:03:47,867
<i> Ma'am, your basket is ready.</i>

88
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:49,800
<i>- It's in the garden.
- Why is that?</i>

89
00:03:49,933 --> 00:03:53,800
<i>Because you always go straight
there when you come here.</i>

90
00:03:53,967 --> 00:03:56,533
<i>Maybe next time, I want to spend
time with them, Nanny.</i>

91
00:03:57,733 --> 00:03:58,567
<i> Sorry, here.</i>

92
00:04:00,133 --> 00:04:01,833
<i> Mom, you keep dropping it!</i>

93
00:04:01,967 --> 00:04:03,600
<i> I'm sorry, I'm sorry.</i>

94
00:04:06,533 --> 00:04:08,000
<i> Nestor!</i>

95
00:04:10,233 --> 00:04:12,800
<i> Secure the gate and perimeter.</i>

96
00:04:12,933 --> 00:04:14,167
<i> Tell the others.</i>

97
00:04:14,300 --> 00:04:15,367
<i> Close the house!</i>

98
00:04:15,500 --> 00:04:17,133
<i> Get them.</i>

99
00:04:17,267 --> 00:04:18,233
<i>- Why?
- No one gets out!</i>

100
00:04:18,367 --> 00:04:19,700
<i>- What? Why?
- What does this mean?</i>

101
00:04:19,833 --> 00:04:22,900
[CLAMORING]

102
00:04:23,033 --> 00:04:25,467
<i> What does this mean?</i>

103
00:04:25,600 --> 00:04:27,367
<i> Did the police follow us?</i>

104
00:04:27,500 --> 00:04:30,333
<i> No! What are you saying?</i>

105
00:04:30,500 --> 00:04:31,833
<i> Boss, Tony texted.</i>

106
00:04:31,967 --> 00:04:33,967
<i>There are police
in the vicinity!</i>

107
00:04:34,400 --> 00:04:36,367
<i> You animal!</i>

108
00:04:36,500 --> 00:04:40,500
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

109
00:04:43,400 --> 00:04:46,533
You betrayed me, Tomas!

110
00:04:46,667 --> 00:04:49,233
Living a double life?
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

111
00:04:49,367 --> 00:04:51,167
Leading a syndicate?

112
00:04:52,133 --> 00:04:56,800
Everything about you is a lie!

113
00:04:56,933 --> 00:04:58,833
Do you really want
to go against me?

114
00:05:00,400 --> 00:05:01,700
[PHONE CHIMES]

115
00:05:07,567 --> 00:05:09,300
Tell the others.

116
00:05:13,500 --> 00:05:17,367
- [GUNS FIRING IN DISTANCE]
- [TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

117
00:05:17,500 --> 00:05:20,300
[JOEY GRUNTING]

118
00:05:20,433 --> 00:05:24,467
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

119
00:05:33,067 --> 00:05:35,267
Major, my family
is in danger inside.

120
00:05:35,433 --> 00:05:38,067
You know what Tomas
can do to them!

121
00:05:38,200 --> 00:05:41,600
[GUNS FIRING IN THE DISTANCE]

122
00:05:41,733 --> 00:05:45,833
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

123
00:05:51,667 --> 00:05:54,233
[BULLETS PLINKING]

124
00:05:54,367 --> 00:05:58,333
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

125
00:06:07,933 --> 00:06:09,900
[PHONE RINGING]

126
00:06:11,733 --> 00:06:12,933
Yvette!

127
00:06:13,067 --> 00:06:14,633
Brother-in-law...

128
00:06:14,767 --> 00:06:16,200
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

129
00:06:16,333 --> 00:06:17,733
You animal!

130
00:06:17,867 --> 00:06:19,233
<i> What did you do to my family?</i>

131
00:06:19,367 --> 00:06:20,367
Release them!

132
00:06:20,500 --> 00:06:23,067
<i>They're my family too,
remember, Andrew.</i>

133
00:06:23,200 --> 00:06:26,367
[MAIDS SOBBING]

134
00:06:26,500 --> 00:06:28,033
[SHRIEKING]

135
00:06:28,167 --> 00:06:30,000
[GUN FIRING]

136
00:06:30,133 --> 00:06:32,533
I won't hurt them...

137
00:06:32,667 --> 00:06:34,033
<i> for now.</i>

138
00:06:34,167 --> 00:06:36,600
So, tell Major Delgado...

139
00:06:36,733 --> 00:06:38,667
<i>to leave.
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]</i>

140
00:06:38,800 --> 00:06:41,400
If not, someone will die
here again.

141
00:06:42,700 --> 00:06:45,967
Tomas, this won't help
your situation!

142
00:06:46,100 --> 00:06:47,033
Surrender now!

143
00:06:47,167 --> 00:06:49,033
<i>Don't make it harder
for yourself!</i>

144
00:06:49,833 --> 00:06:53,233
I built my empire for decades,
Major.

145
00:06:53,367 --> 00:06:56,100
<i>I invested sweat and blood
in this business.</i>

146
00:06:56,233 --> 00:06:58,200
From small deals,

147
00:06:58,333 --> 00:07:00,467
to life-threatening
transactions.

148
00:07:00,600 --> 00:07:02,700
<i> But the way you're talking,</i>

149
00:07:02,833 --> 00:07:05,467
it's like you're asking me
to close a small store.

150
00:07:05,600 --> 00:07:08,267
<i>That's the problem with the dead
who came back...</i>

151
00:07:08,400 --> 00:07:11,400
<i>a screw is missing in the brain.</i>

152
00:07:12,767 --> 00:07:14,333
This is what should happen.

153
00:07:14,500 --> 00:07:18,333
<i>First, you will all leave
the compound.</i>

154
00:07:18,467 --> 00:07:21,700
Second, I will only talk to you.

155
00:07:21,833 --> 00:07:25,133
<i>If I hear even a hint
of noise...</i>

156
00:07:26,500 --> 00:07:27,867
or if anyone disobeys...

157
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:29,733
someone will die in here.

158
00:07:33,067 --> 00:07:35,033
And last condition,

159
00:07:35,167 --> 00:07:37,267
<i> I need a vehicle...</i>

160
00:07:37,400 --> 00:07:40,333
<i>with two fully-loaded long arms.</i>

161
00:07:40,467 --> 00:07:43,967
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

162
00:07:44,767 --> 00:07:49,200
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

163
00:07:59,533 --> 00:08:03,567
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

164
00:08:14,100 --> 00:08:15,500
Hey!

165
00:08:17,833 --> 00:08:19,567
Where are you going?

166
00:08:20,700 --> 00:08:24,233
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

167
00:08:24,633 --> 00:08:26,233
[UNEASY MUSIC CONTINUES]

168
00:08:28,767 --> 00:08:30,367
Put that down!

169
00:08:30,500 --> 00:08:32,700
[UNEASY MUSIC CONTINUES]

170
00:08:32,833 --> 00:08:34,467
Are you crazy, Tomas?

171
00:08:34,600 --> 00:08:36,800
We won't give you weapons!

172
00:08:36,933 --> 00:08:37,833
No!

173
00:08:37,967 --> 00:08:39,867
<i> Major...</i>

174
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:42,200
I can't be at a disadvantage.

175
00:08:42,767 --> 00:08:44,233
<i> You already cornered me here.</i>

176
00:08:44,367 --> 00:08:46,400
If you don't give me my demands,

177
00:08:46,533 --> 00:08:49,033
no one will get out of here.

178
00:08:49,500 --> 00:08:50,567
[GRUNTS]

179
00:08:50,700 --> 00:08:52,133
[THUDS]

180
00:08:53,100 --> 00:08:54,000
[CLACKS]

181
00:08:54,133 --> 00:08:55,767
Come here!

182
00:08:56,300 --> 00:08:59,300
- [THUDDING]
- [TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

183
00:08:59,433 --> 00:09:01,200
- [THUDS]
- [GOON GROANS]

184
00:09:02,733 --> 00:09:05,833
- [THUDDING]
- [GROANING]

185
00:09:05,967 --> 00:09:08,300
[CRASHES AND RATTLES]

186
00:09:11,767 --> 00:09:15,300
[GUNS FIRING IN DISTANCE]

187
00:09:15,433 --> 00:09:19,033
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

188
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:22,000
You already know
you're at a disadvantage!

189
00:09:22,133 --> 00:09:24,367
Why don't you surrender?

190
00:09:24,500 --> 00:09:25,500
What, Tomas?

191
00:09:25,633 --> 00:09:26,800
<i> Don't involve others!</i>

192
00:09:26,933 --> 00:09:28,833
Stop your cruelty!

193
00:09:29,000 --> 00:09:32,067
- [GUN FIRING]
- [CROWD SHRIEKING]

194
00:09:32,200 --> 00:09:33,033
Mom!

195
00:09:33,167 --> 00:09:36,567
[BAWLING]

196
00:09:36,700 --> 00:09:38,800
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

197
00:09:42,067 --> 00:09:43,333
You're an animal, Berdugo!
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

198
00:09:43,633 --> 00:09:45,967
[MAIDS SOBBING]

199
00:09:53,567 --> 00:09:55,700
Relax, Brother-in-law.

200
00:09:55,833 --> 00:09:57,500
<i> Your family is still alive.</i>

201
00:09:57,633 --> 00:10:00,200
However, no one will take care
of your mother anymore.

202
00:10:00,633 --> 00:10:01,933
<i> See?</i>

203
00:10:02,100 --> 00:10:04,633
<i> I kept my end of the deal.</i>

204
00:10:04,767 --> 00:10:07,667
If anyone makes noise,
someone dies.

205
00:10:09,033 --> 00:10:11,233
<i> Now, it's your turn...</i>

206
00:10:11,367 --> 00:10:13,133
<i> to do what I asked.</i>

207
00:10:13,600 --> 00:10:15,400
And I promise...

208
00:10:15,533 --> 00:10:19,167
no noise, no one dies.

209
00:10:19,300 --> 00:10:23,200
[UNEASY MUSIC CONTINUES]

210
00:10:26,200 --> 00:10:28,633
All right, Tomas,
I'll grant your request,

211
00:10:28,767 --> 00:10:30,767
but on one condition.

212
00:10:30,900 --> 00:10:33,367
You won't kill
any of your hostages.

213
00:10:33,500 --> 00:10:36,067
You don't make the conditions,
Major.

214
00:10:36,233 --> 00:10:39,200
But fine, I'll allow it.

215
00:10:40,400 --> 00:10:42,800
But you only have 10 minutes.

216
00:10:42,933 --> 00:10:44,667
<i> When 10 minutes are up</i>

217
00:10:44,800 --> 00:10:47,000
<i> and I don't get what I asked,</i>

218
00:10:47,133 --> 00:10:48,900
<i> someone dies again here.</i>

219
00:10:49,033 --> 00:10:50,933
<i> 10 minutes, one life.</i>

220
00:10:51,067 --> 00:10:52,933
Tomas! They're your family...

221
00:10:53,067 --> 00:10:55,367
[PHONE BEEPING]

222
00:10:55,500 --> 00:10:59,633
[SINISTER MUSIC PLAYING]

223
00:11:02,500 --> 00:11:05,333
[SOBBING]

224
00:11:05,467 --> 00:11:08,667
Please...

225
00:11:09,333 --> 00:11:12,167
[SOBBING]

226
00:11:16,600 --> 00:11:17,933
What?

227
00:11:18,067 --> 00:11:19,767
Is this the first time
you've seen me like this?

228
00:11:19,900 --> 00:11:22,267
That I'm different
from how you knew me?

229
00:11:24,100 --> 00:11:26,533
Say it, it's okay.

230
00:11:26,667 --> 00:11:31,600
I regret marrying a demon!

231
00:11:32,433 --> 00:11:34,833
Well, you know what they say.

232
00:11:34,967 --> 00:11:38,433
When you marry evil,
you become part of it.

233
00:11:40,167 --> 00:11:42,233
You're not so innocent, Yvette.

234
00:11:43,067 --> 00:11:45,167
You benefitted from me too.

235
00:11:45,967 --> 00:11:49,000
You got your charity works
from my business.

236
00:11:50,067 --> 00:11:51,600
I wouldn't have accepted it

237
00:11:51,733 --> 00:11:54,933
if I knew it came
from evil deeds, Tomas!

238
00:11:55,067 --> 00:11:56,233
No!

239
00:11:56,367 --> 00:12:02,667
[PHONE RINGING]

240
00:12:03,767 --> 00:12:06,900
[SINISTER MUSIC PLAYING]

241
00:12:07,033 --> 00:12:08,833
They took the bait.

242
00:12:08,967 --> 00:12:10,900
Get ready for extraction.

243
00:12:12,767 --> 00:12:14,533
What's that?

244
00:12:14,700 --> 00:12:17,900
You made a deal with the police,
but you have another plan?

245
00:12:18,433 --> 00:12:20,800
That's the problem with Delgado.

246
00:12:20,933 --> 00:12:22,600
He is gullible.

247
00:12:23,133 --> 00:12:24,500
This is my home court,

248
00:12:24,633 --> 00:12:27,167
so I decide who lives,

249
00:12:27,300 --> 00:12:29,233
who dies,

250
00:12:29,367 --> 00:12:31,033
and who escapes.

251
00:12:32,633 --> 00:12:33,933
Now...

252
00:12:34,067 --> 00:12:39,500
shut up or else I won't bring
the children back here!

253
00:12:42,067 --> 00:12:43,500
Good choice.

254
00:12:43,633 --> 00:12:47,400
[SINISTER MUSIC CONTINUES]

255
00:12:47,800 --> 00:12:52,167
When you're done,
bring the children back here.

256
00:12:55,233 --> 00:12:59,167
If Berdugo agrees,
we can execute plan A.

257
00:12:59,300 --> 00:13:01,067
The vehicle is on its way,
Major.

258
00:13:01,200 --> 00:13:02,367
Good.

259
00:13:02,500 --> 00:13:04,167
Our priority is...

260
00:13:04,300 --> 00:13:06,667
to keep Berdugo away
from his hostages.

261
00:13:07,233 --> 00:13:09,667
Major, I don't think
he'll keep his word.

262
00:13:15,500 --> 00:13:18,567
This is the only way
to save your family.

263
00:13:18,700 --> 00:13:20,600
We need to take the risk.

264
00:13:22,067 --> 00:13:24,400
All units, move out!

265
00:13:28,833 --> 00:13:32,833
[INTENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

266
00:13:33,567 --> 00:13:35,067
Let's go!

267
00:13:35,200 --> 00:13:39,167
[INTENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

268
00:13:46,467 --> 00:13:50,667
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

269
00:13:58,067 --> 00:13:59,267
My grandchildren!

270
00:13:59,400 --> 00:14:02,633
[CLAMORING]

271
00:14:02,767 --> 00:14:05,300
Are you okay? Kisses?

272
00:14:05,433 --> 00:14:09,200
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

273
00:14:22,633 --> 00:14:26,600
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

274
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:43,500
[PHONE BUZZING]

275
00:14:45,867 --> 00:14:46,900
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

276
00:14:47,033 --> 00:14:47,800
Joey?

277
00:14:47,933 --> 00:14:49,033
<i> Hello, Jin Ho?</i>

278
00:14:49,167 --> 00:14:50,900
Do not tell anyone that I'm
the one you're talking to.

279
00:14:51,033 --> 00:14:52,367
Okay, I'm listening.

280
00:14:53,800 --> 00:14:58,067
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

281
00:14:59,333 --> 00:15:00,833
Jin Ho!

282
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:02,000
Joey!

283
00:15:05,200 --> 00:15:06,867
They are inside.

284
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:08,367
We can't get them
all out at once

285
00:15:08,500 --> 00:15:10,200
without being noticed.

286
00:15:15,933 --> 00:15:17,633
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

287
00:15:24,700 --> 00:15:28,633
[PHONE KEYS CLICKING]

288
00:15:33,833 --> 00:15:35,833
[PHONE CHIMES]

289
00:15:37,300 --> 00:15:39,133
Cruz, stay alert.

290
00:15:39,267 --> 00:15:41,933
Watch out for the vehicle.
[PHONE BUZZES]

291
00:15:50,400 --> 00:15:52,700
[PHONE BUZZES]

292
00:15:52,833 --> 00:15:57,267
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

293
00:15:58,000 --> 00:16:00,667
Major, I think it's time
we execute plan B.

294
00:16:00,800 --> 00:16:04,933
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

295
00:16:09,833 --> 00:16:11,000
Here, I already reset the modem

296
00:16:11,133 --> 00:16:12,767
while the LAN cables
were on the second port.

297
00:16:12,900 --> 00:16:14,467
Then?

298
00:16:15,800 --> 00:16:18,300
Ah, there, it's green now.
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

299
00:16:18,433 --> 00:16:20,267
All right, Kyle. Thank you.

300
00:16:23,167 --> 00:16:24,467
Kyle!

301
00:16:24,600 --> 00:16:27,833
But, Kyle, why didn't you rebook
your ticket?

302
00:16:27,967 --> 00:16:28,833
Fine, it's your family.

303
00:16:28,967 --> 00:16:30,600
All right,
just bring something home.

304
00:16:30,733 --> 00:16:31,733
Nice.

305
00:16:31,867 --> 00:16:33,533
Thank you, bye.

306
00:16:34,967 --> 00:16:35,733
This is good now.

307
00:16:35,867 --> 00:16:37,600
The connection is stable.

308
00:16:37,733 --> 00:16:39,700
Right. Thanks, Peter.

309
00:16:39,833 --> 00:16:42,667
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

310
00:16:42,833 --> 00:16:44,700
Still no word from Joey?

311
00:16:45,167 --> 00:16:46,700
None.

312
00:16:47,133 --> 00:16:48,167
Better not contact her anymore.

313
00:16:48,300 --> 00:16:49,667
It might make things worse.

314
00:16:51,000 --> 00:16:52,767
[PHONE CHIMES]

315
00:16:53,900 --> 00:16:55,733
Peter...

316
00:16:56,400 --> 00:16:58,233
Andrew said we're starting.

317
00:16:58,367 --> 00:17:02,433
[INTENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

318
00:17:12,600 --> 00:17:16,733
[INTENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

319
00:17:18,667 --> 00:17:20,900
Sir, the vehicle is here.

320
00:17:21,033 --> 00:17:22,300
<i> Good.</i>

321
00:17:22,433 --> 00:17:26,400
[INTENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

322
00:17:43,000 --> 00:17:44,833
[PHONE RINGING]

323
00:17:45,233 --> 00:17:49,800
[PHONE BUZZING]

324
00:17:49,967 --> 00:17:52,733
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

325
00:17:52,867 --> 00:17:54,900
Berdugo, this is Delgado.

326
00:17:55,033 --> 00:17:57,067
Major, is there a problem?

327
00:17:57,200 --> 00:17:59,033
Your request is here.

328
00:17:59,167 --> 00:18:03,300
[UNEASY MUSIC CONTINUES]

329
00:18:11,867 --> 00:18:13,433
It's here, Sir.

330
00:18:13,567 --> 00:18:17,567
[UNEASY MUSIC CONTINUES]

331
00:18:22,967 --> 00:18:25,733
Are you sure we can trust
what you brought?

332
00:18:25,867 --> 00:18:27,467
Then check it out yourself!

333
00:18:29,767 --> 00:18:31,333
Release your hostages!

334
00:18:31,467 --> 00:18:33,100
<i> Easy.</i>

335
00:18:33,233 --> 00:18:35,667
<i> We'll get there, Major.</i>

336
00:18:35,800 --> 00:18:38,633
How long will you hide
behind your hostages?

337
00:18:38,767 --> 00:18:40,600
<i>Behind your own family?
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]</i>

338
00:18:41,133 --> 00:18:43,300
Is that the Berdugo
everyone fears?

339
00:18:44,467 --> 00:18:46,400
<i> I really admire you, Andrew.</i>

340
00:18:47,833 --> 00:18:50,167
<i>You and Rebecca
are exactly alike.</i>

341
00:18:50,300 --> 00:18:53,100
<i>I admire how frank
your words are.</i>

342
00:18:53,667 --> 00:18:56,933
That's why I really want you
out of my way.

343
00:18:57,467 --> 00:19:00,633
You're lucky,
you only got beaten up.

344
00:19:00,767 --> 00:19:02,267
[INTENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

345
00:19:02,400 --> 00:19:06,733
- [THUDDING]
- [ANDREW GROANING]

346
00:19:09,100 --> 00:19:10,433
You animal!

347
00:19:11,133 --> 00:19:12,600
So, you were behind that?

348
00:19:12,733 --> 00:19:13,833
<i> Well...</i>

349
00:19:13,967 --> 00:19:15,767
<i>you're really good,
Brotherinlaw.</i>

350
00:19:15,900 --> 00:19:17,933
You fooled us for so long,

351
00:19:18,067 --> 00:19:20,133
even the police.

352
00:19:20,267 --> 00:19:22,467
You were like an urban legend,

353
00:19:22,600 --> 00:19:24,600
<i> disguised as Berdugo.</i>

354
00:19:24,733 --> 00:19:26,933
I'll take that as a compliment

355
00:19:27,067 --> 00:19:31,267
coming from a brave journalist
like you.

356
00:19:33,433 --> 00:19:37,567
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

357
00:19:46,867 --> 00:19:48,667
[INTENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

358
00:19:48,800 --> 00:19:51,900
Hush, calm down.
[MOUTHS]

359
00:20:02,200 --> 00:20:03,600
So, tell me, Berdugo...
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

360
00:20:04,500 --> 00:20:06,700
How many tons of drugs
have you sold

361
00:20:06,833 --> 00:20:08,933
and how many lives have you
destroyed?

362
00:20:10,133 --> 00:20:12,500
I'm just a businessman, Andrew.

363
00:20:13,867 --> 00:20:16,000
Don't put all the blame on me.

364
00:20:16,133 --> 00:20:17,700
<i> I'm just the seller.</i>

365
00:20:17,833 --> 00:20:21,467
It's still up to them
if they buy or not,

366
00:20:21,600 --> 00:20:24,433
if they want to be
junkies or not.

367
00:20:24,567 --> 00:20:27,967
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

368
00:20:28,867 --> 00:20:31,233
Berdugo is insane!

369
00:20:31,367 --> 00:20:32,367
It's all your fault!

370
00:20:32,500 --> 00:20:33,833
Madman!

371
00:20:35,667 --> 00:20:37,133
Hey...

372
00:20:37,267 --> 00:20:39,267
wait, wait, is this a glitch?

373
00:20:39,400 --> 00:20:40,267
The live suddenly hit
100,000 views.

374
00:20:40,400 --> 00:20:41,900
Look, there's so many!

375
00:20:42,033 --> 00:20:43,367
What did you do?

376
00:20:43,500 --> 00:20:45,100
The usual.

377
00:20:45,233 --> 00:20:49,500
I contacted journalists
and influencer contacts.

378
00:20:49,633 --> 00:20:51,167
Solid.

379
00:20:54,533 --> 00:20:58,567
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

380
00:21:05,900 --> 00:21:07,133
[CLICKS]

381
00:21:07,267 --> 00:21:10,233
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

382
00:21:17,333 --> 00:21:19,300
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

383
00:21:19,433 --> 00:21:22,100
[MOUTHS INDISTINCTLY]

384
00:21:31,467 --> 00:21:35,667
[UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]

385
00:21:37,700 --> 00:21:38,733
Isn't that poetic?

386
00:21:38,867 --> 00:21:40,567
That I was the one
who gave you a medal

387
00:21:40,700 --> 00:21:42,100
for being my valiant savior?

388
00:21:42,267 --> 00:21:42,900
You talk too much!

389
00:21:43,033 --> 00:21:44,033
Let's end this!

390
00:21:44,167 --> 00:21:45,667
Joey, Jin Ho,
Berdugo is coming back.

391
00:21:45,800 --> 00:21:46,967
Joey, where are you?

392
00:21:47,100 --> 00:21:48,500
I need your help.

393
00:21:48,633 --> 00:21:49,533
Let's go to the hangar.

394
00:21:49,667 --> 00:21:50,833
The pilot is on the way,
Berdugo.

395
00:21:50,967 --> 00:21:51,900
What's that? A live?

396
00:21:52,033 --> 00:21:53,700
Boss, someone's chasing us.

397
00:21:53,833 --> 00:21:54,800
Guys, help us.

398
00:21:54,933 --> 00:21:56,900
Pass this to the police
or to Tirada Express.

399
00:21:57,033 --> 00:21:59,100
Berdugo's vehicle
is right in front of me.

400
00:22:00,267 --> 00:22:01,767
<i> Tirada</i> and<i> Saludo</i> viewers...

401
00:22:01,900 --> 00:22:03,133
I'm not Boss Idol,

402
00:22:03,267 --> 00:22:04,867
but we have only one mission...

403
00:22:05,000 --> 00:22:06,867
and that is to capture Berdugo.
